    "durationMs": 318967,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built:\n\n**Stack**: Spring Boot 3.4.5 / Java 21, Spring Data JPA, Flyway + PostgreSQL 16.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `POST /links` — validates `url` (absolute http/https with host via `java.net.URI`), optional `code` matching `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`; generates an 8-char random code when omitted. Returns 201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, URL stored/returned exactly as submitted. Duplicate custom code → 409 (pre-check + unique-constraint catch for races).\n- `GET /links/{code}` → 200 or 404; `GET /links` → `{items, total}` ordered by id (creation order).\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with `Location`, increments clicks via an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1` query — 20 concurrent redirects yielded exactly 20 clicks.\n- 422 for malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, invalid code — via a `@RestControllerAdvice` mapping every error to `{\"error\": \"...\"}` JSON.\n- `DATABASE_URL` (postgresql://) is translated to JDBC settings by an `EnvironmentPostProcessor`; no hard-coded credentials.\n- `sh start.sh` execs the prebuilt fat jar in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; Flyway applies pending migrations at startup (idempotent on restart).\n\n**Verified live**: all 24 curl checks passed, including data and click counts surviving a full server restart."
  }
